1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,120
SME Quote Dashboard: which quotes came back signed, and what has been billed.

2
00:00:05,672 --> 00:00:12,322
It replaced a Power BI report that everyone needed a licence for, rebuilt by hand from one Excel register.

3
00:00:12,875 --> 00:00:22,335
Now an Azure Function reads the register and three lead trackers from SharePoint, and writes one private data file. Staff sign in with their company account.

4
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:28,390
The Quote Report shows the acceptance rate and signed-back value, this year against last.

5
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:32,495
Click any bar, and every chart on the page follows.

6
00:00:33,046 --> 00:00:38,906
The Quote Tree breaks the value down by year, agent, and service, one click at a time.

7
00:00:39,457 --> 00:00:45,027
Quote versus Billing shows contract value, what has been billed, and what is left to bill.

8
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:49,590
One press of Refresh rebuilds every figure in about a minute.

9
00:00:50,146 --> 00:00:54,366
SME Quote Dashboard. A demo with made-up data.
